<speak>A pile can look very orderly until someone needs the page at the bottom. A labelled box sounds easier to share, especially if both of you use the same names for things. You don't have to make it elaborate. A cover sheet saying what belongs in each section can be enough. For electronic copies, the same folder names as the physical box may help, so you aren't mentally translating between two different filing systems whenever you move from the desk to the computer.</speak>